  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It authorises spending up to a stated amount for a stated purpose.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    80,000,000 − 74,000,000 = ₦6,000,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is not a profit; the regulations decide what happens to it.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The excess has not been authorised, so further approval is needed.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Receipts and payments are recorded when the money moves.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Economy, efficiency and effectiveness are the tests of whether the money was well used.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Economy is about the price paid for the input.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Efficiency compares output with the resources consumed.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Effectiveness asks whether the intended result was achieved.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The audit exists to assure the legislature that the money was spent as authorised.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Each fund has its own books and its own rules.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The development fund is for capital expenditure.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The contingency fund meets emergencies with approval.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A trust fund may be used only for the purpose of the trust.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Each fund is spent only on its own purpose, which is the point of fund accounting.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Virement allows a saving on one line to be applied to another, but only with authority.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    One posting creates both entries, which is why the trial balance is automatic.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
